{"text": "DAVE CAVELL\ndave@davecavell.com\n\nEDUCATION\n\nGeorgetown University Law Center Washington, DC May 2013\nJuris Doctor\ne Journal Membership: Georgetown Journal of Legal Ethics, Executive Development Editor\ne Publications: Note, Ghetto Loans: Discrimination Against Black Borrowers in Mortgage Markets and\nthe Impact of the Ibanez Decision, 25 GEO. J. LEGAL Etuics 449 (Summer 2012).\n[Note that \"ghetto loans\" is the terminology used by Wells Fargo, per testimony from a former employee, as I note in the\n\npiece.]\n\nTufts University Medford, MA May 2006\nBachelor of Arts in Political Science\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nDave Cavell for United States Congress Brookline, MA Oct. 2019 to Present\nCandidate in Massachusetts 4\u00b0\" Congressional District\ne Running to represent 750,000 4\" District residents in Congress\ne Oversee 15 staff & 100 volunteers, speak regularly in public, participate in debates & media interviews\nOffice of Attorney General Maura Healey Boston, MA Feb. 2017 to Sept. 2019\nSenior Advisor and Assistant Attorney General\ne Advised AG Healey on communications and legal strategy, policy initiatives, and upcoming events\ne Part of the team that sued President Trump over 50 times, including to stop the Muslim travel ban, to\n\ndefend the Affordable Care Act, and to end the family separation policy at the southern border\ne Part of the team that sued the NRA, Exxon Mobil, and launched the nation-leading case against Purdue\n\nPharma\ne Supervised and managed team of employees and interns who plan, organize, and staff all external events\nThe White House Washington, DC Sept. 2015 to Jan. 2017\n\nPresidential Speechwriter\ne Worked directly with President Barack Obama and First Lady Michelle Obama to research, write, and edit\nspeeches, including major policy addresses, Weekly Addresses, and award presentations\n\nChoate, Hall & Stewart LLP Boston, MA Jan. 2014 to Aug. 2015\nLitigation Associate\ne Worked with complex commercial litigation teams to prepare for trial and research legal issues\nOffice of Governor Deval Patrick Boston, MA Aug. 2007 to Nov. 2010\nDeputy Speechwriter and Deputy Director of New Media\ne Wrote speeches and opinion editorials for Governor Deval Patrick and other Cabinet officials\ne Hired and supervised over 30 communications interns, worked as part of Senior Communications Team\nNew York City Elementary School PS28X South Bronx, NY Jul. 2006 to Jul. 2007\n\n4\" Grade Homeroom Teacher\ne Taught 32 English Language Learner students English, Social Studies, and Math",
